        "pattern, where:",
        "Pattern ignoreCase=\"true\">/a/*/{id}</Pattern> <Pattern ignoreCase=\"true\">/a/**/{id}</Pattern> </URIPath>",
        "pattern matches requests with pathsuffixes (the portion of the URI path following the basepath) such as \"/a/b/c\", \"/a/foo/bar\", etc.",
        "pattern matches any number of path segments after \"/a/\", such as \"/a/foo/bar/baz/c\", as well as \"/a/b/c\" and \"/a/foo/bar\".",
        "pattern as:",
        "pattern matches the values \"text/xml;charset=UTF-16\" and \"application/xml;charset=ASCII\".",
        "pattern because they are used as literal characters in the value of the query parameter:",
        "Pattern ignoreCase=\"true\">%{user%} {name}</Pattern> </QueryParam>",
        "pattern matches the value \"{user} Steve\" but not the value \"user Steve\"."
      ]
